{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>All that YHWH has spoken we will do.</b> They acknowledged and accepted upon themselves the yoke of Torah and the commandments and did so willingly. And what our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted — that He suspended the mountain over them like a tub and said to them, 'If you accept the Torah, well and good; and if not, there shall be your burial' — concerns the Oral Torah, which contains warnings and punishments and many fences and hedges; but the Written Torah they all acknowledged of their own will, with great desire, in joy and gladness of heart, and required no coercion — only in the Oral Torah." "<b>And Moses returned.</b> Some explained that he brought the reply in his hand and did not manage to deliver it until the word of the Omnipresent was revealed upon him, as it says, 'Behold, I come to you in the thickness of the cloud,' etc., and then he delivered it — and this is 'and Moses reported.' And it is possible to interpret that 'and Moses returned' refers to their saying 'we will do,' while 'and Moses reported' is what they demanded, for they wanted to hear from His mouth, blessed be He; and the sense is that two things were joined together, one of which is explicitly stated in the verse and the other is not stated. And Israel, who demanded this, found an opening in the words of the Omnipresent, who said, 'If you will surely hearken to My voice'; therefore, when Moses brought back the answer 'we will do,' the Holy One, blessed be He, said to him, 'so that the people may hear' — and then 'and Moses reported': the hearing from His mouth is what they were demanding. And so we find in the Midrash at the beginning of Shir HaShirim Rabbah, on the verse 'and Moses reported the words of the people to YHWH' — that they said: 'We wish to hear from His mouth; we desire to see our King.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:01:07.038380568Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}